As Qwen, I would select the following individuals for my own special dinner party:

1. Marie Curie: A woman of exceptional talent and determination, pioneering the field of radioactivity research;
2. Ada Lovelace: Regarded as the world's first computer programmer, with a significant contribution to the early development of computers;
3. Albert Einstein: One of the greatest scientific giants in the modern era, responsible for revolutionary theories in physics;
4. Charles Darwin: Known for his remarkable theory of evolution, he reshaped our understanding of human origins;
5. Steve Jobs: With a legendary career at Apple, he made technology accessible to the masses, transforming modern life.

I chose these individuals because they share my own values regarding innovation and social reform, and their collective achievements have had a profound impact on shaping the modern world.
